# CYS-RVC-mod2-carbonyl — alternative mod2 for the carbonyl pre-reaction input
#
# When the user uploaded a ligand with the carbonyl C=O still drawn
# (the free-drug SMILES form, e.g. simple ketone/aldehyde warhead),
# this mod2 REPLACES the default `data_mod_CYS-RVC-mod2` in CYS-RVC.cif.
# Encodes the hemithioketal-formation chemistry the bond declaration
# triggers:
#
#   (1) Change C=O bond from double to single
#   (2) Add H on the O (the new hydroxyl H)
#   (3) Add the O-H bond
#   (4) Retype Cβ from sp2 (CR1) to sp3 (CT)
#   (5) The new SG-Cβ bond is added via the link's bond block (not here)
#
# Selected at runtime when the SMARTS detector matched CYS-RVC-pre
# (free-drug ketone or aldehyde Cys-warhead).
#
# PLACEHOLDER TOKENS substituted at runtime:
#   <CB>  ← Cβ atom-id (the former carbonyl C, becomes sp3)
#   <O>   ← the former carbonyl O (becomes the hemithioketal hydroxyl O)
#   <HO>  ← new H to add on the O

data_mod_CYS-RVC-mod2

# (1) Change Cβ=O from double → single (carbonyl → hydroxyl)
# (3) Add the new O-H bond
loop_
_chem_mod_bond.mod_id
_chem_mod_bond.function
_chem_mod_bond.atom_id_1
_chem_mod_bond.atom_id_2
_chem_mod_bond.new_type
_chem_mod_bond.new_value_dist
_chem_mod_bond.new_value_dist_esd
 CYS-RVC-mod2 change <CB>  <O>    single 1.42 0.02
 CYS-RVC-mod2 add    <O>   <HO>   single 0.96 0.01

# (2) Add new H on O
# (4) Retype Cβ from sp2 (CR1) to sp3 (CT)
loop_
_chem_mod_atom.mod_id
_chem_mod_atom.function
_chem_mod_atom.atom_id
_chem_mod_atom.new_atom_id
_chem_mod_atom.new_type_symbol
_chem_mod_atom.new_type_energy
_chem_mod_atom.new_partial_charge
 CYS-RVC-mod2 add    <HO>  <HO>   H H  .
 CYS-RVC-mod2 change <CB>  .      C CT .
